Z||000000||MickeyAsh||12-13-2001||04:22 PM||||Okiedoke, as some of you may remember, I spun a bearing on the 2.8... new developements are: I got my '94 Northstar on the way, and I'm eyeing a 4T80E tranny. BUT, the N* is still being shipped to me, so I dont have the engine code off it yet, and I read the 4T80E only bolts onto the N*'s with a "Y" engine code... NOW, my questions are: will the 4T80E bolt on to ALL northstars, or just the Y coded ones? If so, is there any way to modify the 4T80E to fit a non-Y coded N*? And if not, is there any way through pictures for me to determine if my N* is a Y? Thanks.<p>[This message has been edited by MickeyAsh (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jay||12-13-2001||05:19 PM||||I believe it will bolt up, the problem lies in the ecm.  The difference in the engines as you may know, is one is 275 while the other is 300.  Accordingly, the final drive gear ratios are different between the two trannies.  You must match up the ecm with the tranny and engine.  To see my Northstar site goto <A HREF="http://members.rogers.com/jaygrande/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.rogers.com/jaygrande/</A>  The email on the page is wrong but it is in my profile here.  Artherd and Will can also help in this regard.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||12-13-2001||05:20 PM||||Oh yeah, which car did it come out of?  You can tell (sometimes) by which Caddy it came out of.||||reg||1
